een a consistent ceiling across several intraday attempts this past week.\n\nOn the H1 timeframe, the picture is one of a controlled pullback. Price held a tight range through the late Sunday and early Monday hours, clustered around 17.485\u201317.491, before European participants began pressing the pair lower from the 05:00 candle onward. The move from 17.50 to the current 17.436 has been relatively linear, with each hourly close printing below the prior one through the morning. There is no obvious stabilisation candle yet, though the 12:00\u201314:00 range has tightened considerably, suggesting the selling pressure may be losing momentum near the support zone.\n\nToday's calendar is empty of scheduled risk events, which removes a clear catalyst for any sharp directional move. In the absence of data, the pair is likely to remain at the mercy of broader dollar flows and any headline risk around US-Mexico trade dynamics, which have been a persistent background theme for the peso this year.\n\nThe read changes meaningfully on a clean daily close below 17.4324. That would bring the next prior reaction zone at 17.3496 into the structural conversation and would shift the short-term tone toward peso strength. Conversely, a recovery back through 17.50 and a hold above that prior reaction zone would reopen the mid-17.50s and reframe the recent softness as a simple retest of range support rather than the beginning of a directional move lower.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}